From: Dirently
Date: 2026-09-29
Subject: avcodec/mfenc: set CODECAPI_AVLowLatencyMode as a VT_BOOL

CODECAPI_AVLowLatencyMode is a Boolean (VT_BOOL). Microsoft's software
H.264 encoder MFT (Windows' Media Foundation, the encoder h264_mf opens with
hw_encoding=0) refuses the VT_UI4 that mfenc sets with E_INVALIDARG and then
holds 16 frames before its first packet: about 270 ms at 60 frames a second.
As a VT_BOOL it takes it and gives one packet for every frame.

Applied by scripts/build-ffmpeg-windows.sh to the FFmpeg 8.1.3 release.
---
--- a/libavcodec/mfenc.c
+++ b/libavcodec/mfenc.c
@@ -877,8 +877,11 @@
         if (c->opt_enc_scenario >= 0)
             ICodecAPI_SetValue(c->codec_api, &ff_CODECAPI_AVScenarioInfo, FF_VAL_VT_UI4(c->opt_enc_scenario));
 
+        /* Changed for Dirently, 2026-09-29: CODECAPI_AVLowLatencyMode is a
+         * VT_BOOL. Microsoft's H.264 encoder MFT refuses it as VT_UI4
+         * (E_INVALIDARG) and then holds 16 frames before its first packet. */
         if (avctx->flags & AV_CODEC_FLAG_LOW_DELAY)
-            ICodecAPI_SetValue(c->codec_api, &ff_CODECAPI_AVLowLatencyMode, FF_VAL_VT_UI4(1));
+            ICodecAPI_SetValue(c->codec_api, &ff_CODECAPI_AVLowLatencyMode, FF_VAL_VT_BOOL(VARIANT_TRUE));
     }
 
     return 0;
